"""Bet Din cases 85-94: testimony and hearing procedure (BD-192-201)."""
from kehillah_docket_batch40_data import F

EXTRA_CASES_5 = [
 F(85,"BD-192","shopkeepers_son","interest_hidden","nezikin","The Shopkeeper's Son as Witness",
   "[kbd_litigant_a.GetFirstName] calls a young shopkeeper to testify in his father's debt case. [kbd_litigant_b.GetFirstName] says the son stands to inherit the unpaid account. The son's memory is clear, but the family books have not been opened. The court must decide how much weight a close witness can bear.",
   ["Accept the son's account and order payment.","Inspect the books and seek an independent witness.","Exclude the son and dismiss the debt."],
   ["A quick award may rest on a hidden personal interest.","The books and another witness cost time but test the claim.","A reliable account may be lost merely because of kinship."],
   ["The court awards the debt on the son's words.","The court holds the claim and compares the family ledger with outside testimony.","The court excludes the son and closes the account."],
   "The son owns a share of the disputed account. His interest should have been weighed before judgment.",
   "The son has no claim to the account, and independent receipts corroborate him. Dismissal discarded useful proof.",
   "Sanhedrin 3:4","the witness's stake in this particular debt"),
 F(86,"BD-193","hearing_witness","words_misheard","nezikin","The Witness Who Cannot Hear",
   "[kbd_litigant_a.GetFirstName] relies on an elderly witness to a market bargain. [kbd_litigant_b.GetFirstName] says the witness could not hear the price over the crowd. The witness remembers seeing the parties clasp hands. The court must separate what was seen from what was heard.",
   ["Accept the witness's price and enforce the bargain.","Question the witness about sight, hearing and other proof.","Reject the witness's entire account."],
   ["The price is settled quickly, but the witness may have guessed its words.","A careful hearing costs time and may find independent evidence.","A witness who saw the exchange may still provide useful facts."],
   ["The court enforces the price the witness names.","The court asks what the witness heard and what was only seen.","The court refuses all of the witness's evidence."],
   "The witness saw the bargain but misheard its price. Immediate enforcement overstated his knowledge.",
   "He heard the price clearly before the crowd gathered. Total exclusion lost reliable testimony.",
   "Sanhedrin 3:6","which words the witness actually heard"),
 F(87,"BD-194","absent_defendant","agent_unauthorized","nezikin","The Unavailable Defendant",
   "[kbd_litigant_a.GetFirstName] speaks for a trader who left town on the eve of a hearing. [kbd_litigant_b.GetFirstName] is the claimant and fears another delay. A relative offers to answer for the absent trader, but the letter naming that relative is sealed. The court must keep the claim alive without inventing consent.",
   ["Hear the relative as the trader's full agent.","Preserve the claim and verify the letter.","Judge against the trader for failing to appear."],
   ["The case proceeds, but the relative may lack authority to bind the trader.","Verification costs a hearing day but protects both parties.","A validly appointed agent could make default judgment unfair."],
   ["The court lets the relative settle the case.","The court secures the claim and checks the trader's appointment letter.","The court rules against the absent trader."],
   "The letter appoints the relative only to carry documents. A full settlement exceeded the mandate.",
   "The letter clearly authorizes representation. Default judgment ignored a party who had appeared through an agent.",
   "Sanhedrin 3:1","the relative's actual authority"),
 F(88,"BD-195","third_judge","judge_unqualified","nezikin","The Unqualified Third Judge",
   "[kbd_litigant_a.GetFirstName] defends a monetary panel's third judge. [kbd_litigant_b.GetFirstName] says that judge has never studied the rules needed for this case. The first two judges are respected; replacing the third will delay a crowded docket. The court must protect both quorum and competence.",
   ["Keep the panel and hear the case today.","Pause to test qualifications and seat a substitute if needed.","Dissolve every ruling this panel has made."],
   ["Speed may hide a genuine gap in the third judge's competence.","Review costs time but targets the actual concern.","A qualified judge's earlier work could be discarded wholesale."],
   ["The panel proceeds unchanged.","The court checks the third judge's training before this hearing.","The court sets aside the panel's past work."],
   "The third judge lacks the required competence for monetary disputes. Proceeding ignored a real defect.",
   "His training and record are sound. A blanket cancellation punished a valid panel.",
   "Sanhedrin 1:1","this judge's qualifications"),
 F(89,"BD-196","written_confession","clause_inserted","nezikin","The Written Confession",
   "[kbd_litigant_a.GetFirstName] holds a merchant's signed acknowledgment of debt. [kbd_litigant_b.GetFirstName] admits signing, but says a second repayment clause was added later. The ink differs slightly near the margin. The court can secure the principal while asking the scribe and witnesses about that clause.",
   ["Enforce the entire document now.","Secure the principal and examine ink and witnesses.","Discard the document and release all debt."],
   ["A quick award could enforce words added after signature.","Inquiry preserves the undisputed debt while testing the margin.","A sound signed clause might be lost with an overbroad dismissal."],
   ["The court enforces every written term.","The court secures the principal and summons the scribe.","The court dismisses the entire written claim."],
   "The margin was added after the signature. Enforcing it exceeded the merchant's admission.",
   "Witnesses saw the whole text signed. Total dismissal erased a genuine debt.",
   "Shevuot 6:1","when the disputed clause was written"),
 F(90,"BD-197","accounts_oath","record_missing","nezikin","The Oath to Settle Accounts",
   "[kbd_litigant_a.GetFirstName] asks a partner to swear that their accounts are settled. [kbd_litigant_b.GetFirstName] says a crucial cargo page has gone missing and refuses to swear from memory. The bargain called for an oath, but neither party knows whether the absent page would alter the balance.",
   ["Demand the oath and close the accounts.","Secure the claim and search for the cargo page.","Waive the oath and cancel the balance."],
   ["A missing page may make a forced oath unreliable.","A search costs time while preserving both claims.","A complete account might support payment the court would erase."],
   ["The court insists on the oath now.","The court holds the account open and searches the cargo records.","The court cancels the unsettled balance."],
   "The missing page records a disputed shipment. An immediate oath would conceal a material uncertainty.",
   "The page is found and shows an unpaid balance. Cancellation released a real debt.",
   "Shevuot 7:1","what the missing cargo page records"),
 F(91,"BD-198","opposing_courts","other_court_first","nezikin","The Two Courts' Opposing Rulings",
   "[kbd_litigant_a.GetFirstName] brings a local award for a shipment. [kbd_litigant_b.GetFirstName] brings an opposite award from another community. Both seals look sound; the dates are smudged. The court must decide which hearing had authority before collectors take the same goods twice.",
   ["Enforce the local award immediately.","Hold the goods and compare both court records.","Enforce the distant award instead."],
   ["Local pride may outrun an earlier valid hearing elsewhere.","Preserving goods costs time but avoids double enforcement.","The distant court might have ruled after a binding local award."],
   ["The court enforces its local award.","The court holds the shipment while both registers are checked.","The court enforces the distant award."],
   "The distant court heard the claim first with both parties present. Local enforcement ignored that priority.",
   "The local hearing came first and both parties agreed to it. Distant enforcement displaced a settled award.",
   "Sanhedrin 3:1","the sequence and authority of these hearings"),
 F(92,"BD-199","unopened_letter","summary_false","nezikin","The Unopened Letter",
   "[kbd_litigant_a.GetFirstName] carries a sealed letter about a dead merchant's accounts but refuses to open it in court. [kbd_litigant_b.GetFirstName] says the letter may settle an estate debt. The bearer gives a confident summary; the seal belongs to another person. The court needs evidence without making secrecy itself a verdict.",
   ["Accept the bearer's summary as proof.","Preserve the claim and seek lawful disclosure.","Discard the letter and end the dispute."],
   ["The contents may differ from the summary offered aloud.","The court pays to protect the letter and consult those entitled to open it.","An authentic letter could be lost before its proper reader appears."],
   ["The court rules from the bearer's summary.","The court secures the letter and seeks an authorized opening.","The court ignores the letter and closes the claim."],
   "The opened letter contradicts the bearer. His summary would have misled the court.",
   "The letter is authentic and decisive for the estate. Discarding it would have erased proof.",
   "Sanhedrin 4:1","the sealed letter's contents"),
 F(93,"BD-200","benefited_witness","share_promised","nezikin","The Witness Who Benefited",
   "[kbd_litigant_a.GetFirstName] relies on a witness to a disputed property transfer. [kbd_litigant_b.GetFirstName] says the witness was promised a share if the claim succeeds. The promise is said to be in a separate note. The court must learn whether the witness is independent before making his words decide ownership.",
   ["Accept the witness and award the property.","Inspect the note and seek independent proof.","Exclude the witness and dismiss the claim."],
   ["A promised share could color the testimony.","The note and corroboration cost time but address the exact risk.","An independent witness might be discarded on rumor."],
   ["The court awards the claim on the witness's account.","The court asks for the alleged promise and other witnesses.","The court rejects the witness and closes the property case."],
   "A signed note promises the witness part of the property. Immediate reliance ignored his interest.",
   "No promise exists, and other records confirm the transfer. Dismissal threw away sound evidence.",
   "Sanhedrin 3:3","whether the witness was promised a share"),
 F(94,"BD-201","poor_litigant","defense_records_exist","nezikin","The Poor Litigant's Hearing",
   "[kbd_litigant_a.GetFirstName] asks for swift judgment on a loan. [kbd_litigant_b.GetFirstName] is a borrower who cannot pay for copies of old account records. A messenger can fetch them, but the creditor says delay invites evasion. The court must give each side a real hearing without letting poverty become a tactic for endless postponement.",
   ["Judge the debt today on the creditor's papers.","Grant a fixed delay and pay for the records.","Dismiss the creditor's claim for pressing too hard."],
   ["The borrower may have a documented defense no one has seen.","A bounded delay costs the court but preserves both parties' chance to prove their case.","A valid debt could disappear as punishment for impatience."],
   ["The court awards the creditor's demand at once.","The court sets a short deadline and sends for the account copies.","The court dismisses the creditor's claim."],
   "The records include a receipt for part of the debt. Immediate judgment overstated what was owed.",
   "No repayment appears in the records. Dismissal denied a valid claim.",
   "Sanhedrin 4:1","what the borrower's records establish"),
]
